RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
Office of City Clerk
January 12, 2009
The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne met on this date beginning at 6:00 p.m. in
Council Chambers.  Present were: MAYOR - Richard L. Kaysen; COUNCIL MEMBERS - Ms.
Ash, Mr. Brown, Ms. Broyles, Ms. Case, Mr. Collins, Mr. Pierson, Dr. Rinne, Mr. Spiker and
Mr. Valdez.  The pledge of allegiance was recited.

Also present: Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk; Barb Dorr, City Treasurer, and Dan White,
City Attorney.
Consent Agenda. (All agenda items listed with the designation of [CA] are considered to
be routine items by the governing body and will be enacted by one motion.  There will be no
separate discussion on these items unless a member of the governing body so requests and
support by two other members is received.  Any item removed from the Consent Agenda will be
considered in its normal sequence on the agenda.)  Mayor Kaysen announced agenda item #19
(sale of real property to Attention Homes) was being removed from the meeting agenda at the
request of the sponsor, and advised item #10 (Public Hearing to receive input on sale of real
property to Attention Homes) would be affected.  Mr. Pierson moved to approve Consent
Agenda items, seconded by Mr. Brown. Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the
governing body.
 [CA]
MINUTES FROM REGULAR MEETING OF THE GOVERNING BODY ON
DECEMBER 22, 2008.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried.
[CA]
MINUTES FROM SINE DIE SESSION OF THE GOVERNING BODY ON JANUARY
5, 2009.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried.
[CA]
MINUTES FROM THE FIRST REGULAR MEETING OF THE GOVERNING BODY
ON JANUARY 5, 2009.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried.
 [CA]
MINUTES FROM VOUCHERS MEETING OF THE GOVERNING BODY ON
JANUARY 6, 2009.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried.
Mr. Brown moved to approve payment of vouchers as presented, seconded by Mr.
Valdez.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body.
Public hearing to discuss the sale of City-owned real property located at 700 West Fox
Farm Road, Cheyenne, Wyoming to Attention Homes, Inc. which sale will benefit the economic
development of the City of Cheyenne, pursuant to Wyo. Stat. § 15-1-112(b)(i)(D).  The
estimated appraised value of said property to be sold is $184,000 and will be sold to Attention
Homes, Inc. for $2,000.  This land will provide additional space to facilitate the expansion and
redevelopment of Attention Homes, Inc. Dan White, City Attorney, advised the parties involved
were continuing negotiations regarding the sale and indicated the hearing will be rescheduled
