boundaries; county pocket scenario; unknown future development plans for the property, and
infrastructure responsibility and potential costs involving the developer and nearby property
owners.  Ms. Woodhouse introduced James B. Wright, Jb Wright and Associates, Fort Collins,
CO, civil engineer, who provided comments and suggestions regarding the proposed annexation
relative to county pockets/enclave issues, communication with residents in the area,
infrastructure developer responsibilities, reimbursement fees, and future property improvements.
Also expressing concerns with the proposed annexation were John Fafoutakis, Leo Garcia and
Barbara Gjervold.  Topics discussed included: Cost of potential infrastructure improvements to
area property owners and financial burden, and unknown property development plans.  Brad
Emmons, AVI Engineering, agent for the developer, stated the proposed property annexation
alone will not cause creation of a county pocket, and that developer infrastructure
reimbursements are pursuant to city code requirements and no reimbursements for off-site
improvements are being required at this time.  He advised reimbursements may be scheduled in
the future depending on improvements based upon the final plat design, and provided
information on plat requirements, including a traffic study. Mr. Brown moved to approve on
