LEASES/CONTRACTS/LEGAL:
Professional Services Agreement between the City of Cheyenne, and Ziebart Consulting,
LLC, for comprehensive federal government affairs consulting services.  Mr. Valdez moved to
approve in the amount of $4,000.00 per month, seconded by Mr. Collins.  Mr. Valdez moved to
amend by substitute, seconded by Mr. Collins.  Upon inquiry, Deputy City Attorney Erik
Rasmussen advised the substitute amends the section pertaining to binding arbitration to reflect
any litigation would be under the jurisdiction of the First Judicial District Court in Wyoming.
Comments followed in support of the substitute; services available through the state’s
congressional delegation, and consultant reporting concerns. Motion to amend carried.  Voting
“yes” – all members of the governing body.  Main motion as amended by substitute carried.
Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body with the exception of Ms. Case voting “no”.
(#5326)
A Transmission Easement License Agreement between the City of Cheyenne and Silver
Sage Windpower LLC, a Delaware LLC, for transmission of electricity across a certain portion
of the Happy Jack Landfill Property. Mr. Valdez moved to approve, seconded by Mr. Brown.
Mr. Collins moved to amend by substitute, seconded by Ms. Broyles. Nathan Beauheim,
Engineering Services Director, clarified the substitute addresses typographical errors, changes
the time frame in which the easement can be exercised and dollar amounts, and provided
information on revenue to the City pursuant to provisions of the agreement.  Motion to amend
carried.  Voting “yes” –  all members of the governing body with the exception of Ms. Ash
voting “no”.  Comment followed on overhead vs. underground power lines, and potential future
annexation and development of the property.  Main motion as amended by substitute carried.
