Vetter, Interim City Engineer, noted a substitute for amendment had been submitted.  Mr.
Valdez moved to approve, seconded by Mr. Brown. Mr. Valdez moved to postpone for two
weeks (to Jan. 26, 2009), seconded by Mr. Pierson.  It was advised that Finance Committee’s
recommendation to postpone was to allow for re-negotiations with the consultant, which has
occurred since the Committee meeting.  Motion to postpone failed.  Voting “no” – all members
of the governing body.  Mr. Collins moved to amend by substitute agreement, seconded by Mr.
Brown.  Darrell Johnson, AVI, P.C., advised the firm has re-negotiated the scope of work with
City staff and reviewed areas that will result in reduced costs.  Following discussion, motion to
amend carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body.  Main motion as amended by
substitute carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body.  (#5076) Under other City
business, Ms. Broyles expressed appreciation to those involved in negotiations resulting in cost
