ANNOUNCEMENTS/REPORTS/MOTIONS:
Announcement was made that due to the Martin Luther King, Jr., holiday on Monday,
January 19, 2009, Finance Committee will meet at 11:00 a.m. and Public Services Committee
will meet at 12:15 p.m. on Tuesday, January 20, 2009, in Council Meeting Room 122; Vouchers
meeting will be held in Council Chambers at Noon.
Announcement was made of a public hearing to be held January 26, 2009 at 6:00 p.m. in
City Council Chambers to receive comments and input on the proposed sale of real property
owned by the City of Cheyenne, described generally as all those portions of Lots 2, 3 and 4,
Block 553, Original City, Cheyenne, Laramie County, WY (located south of 9 Street and east
th
of Duff Avenue), to Schroll Cabinets, Inc., which sale will benefit the economic development of
the municipality pursuant to Wyo. Stat. §15-1-112(b). The estimated appraised value of said
property to be sold is $3,800.00.
OTHER CITY BUSINESS:
Ms. Broyles announced on Jan. 13, 2009 at 5:00 p.m. at Carey Jr. High School, a public
meeting will be held to discuss plans for the intersection corridor of East Pershing Blvd. located
near Cole Shopping Center.
There being no further business to come before the governing body, the meeting was
officially adjourned at 8:14 p.m.
